Z||000000||FIERO1985||01-29-2001||08:11 PM||||Will this work I want to take plex glass in the shape of the opening for 4x10 cutout and place a 4" mid rockford finatic x and the tweeters to make a plate spaeker? anyone know if it will sound good with my diamond 10" custom in the footwell the gt speakers in the headrest?? will it work??<P><BR>thanks <BR><P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||01-29-2001||09:10 PM||||Yes, that will sound great!. Thats about the best setup to go with. One question though, why plexi? If there is no real reason, then I would just use 1/8 ply and paint it. If your going to best possible sound, take the dash out, and seal them to the bottem of the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||01-30-2001||02:03 AM||||Don't use plexiglass. It will vibrate and cause distortion. Used 1/8" or 1/4" plywood.<BR>I am using Polk Audio 4" components at all four corners. (Dash and Sail panels) I should have pics up next week of the sail panel woofers.<BR>See pics below for what I did. (1/4" plywood)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/speaker1.jpg"> <P>Sail Panel Tweeters.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tweeters.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||01-30-2001||02:22 AM||||Hey Oreif..... Are you doing the sub like Scott has too??<P>P.S. Lookin good  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!!!"</B>||||reg||7
Z||000004||Oreif||01-30-2001||02:33 AM||||Haze, I am just going with 1 8" RF sub. I'm thinking of the stock sub location or footwell. I was thinking under the dash near thw bottom, pointing at an angle. That way it won't be seen or restict foot space. I have to finish the other stuff before I figure where I want the sub. I don't really want it behind the seat.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||01-30-2001||09:07 AM||||Those tweeter's in the rear sail's look great. Is the stereo installed in the car? How does that sound? I used 4" woofers and 7/8" tweet's in the back, but they are both under the speaker cover. I like Oreif's idea because it will remove it from behind a restrictive (stock) speaker cover, moves it out further then stock, and puts it up higher above the headrest's on the seats. Might have to give that one a try some time. Did your tweeter grills come that color, or did you have to paint them? Mine are black, so Im a little curious. I see they have the Polk Audio badge on them. If you painted them, did one hell of a good job.<P>If theres somthing, like good looks, your trying to acomplish with useing plexi, you might want to try fiberglass if your good at it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||overlord||01-30-2001||09:08 AM||||hey oreif,<BR>how exactly did you get the right size of template for the front speakers?<BR>Is there some obvious way to do it that im missing?<BR>And if i went to a setup like that (4inch and a tweeter), from my kenwood 4*10's,  would there be much of a difference?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||01-30-2001||10:20 AM||||Seanh ~ The stereo system isn't completed yet. I'm working on installing the 4" woofers in the sail panels. The tweeters were painted with "Gunship Gray" model paint, then I used an X-acto knife to scrape off the gray from the raised logo.<P>Overlord ~ I just took a stock 4 X 10 and traced the shape onto wood. Then traced the holes for the woofer and tweeter. I cut everything out. Then I just fitted them in by trimming the wood to fit correctly. Painted wood, mounted speakers, and mounted plate. Going to a 4" component system from a 4 X 10 you'll get better mids and better highs but loose bass. Hence the need for a subwoofer. But if you get an 8" or 10" sub, crossover the speakers at 100hz it sounds great. The system I am installing is simular to a system in a friend car so I have an idea what it'll sound like. I'm just doing things alittle different. He had 4 X 6 plates (3.5" woofer with seperate tweet) and I'm using 4" all the way around. I am also installing a digital surround sound processor to aid in staging and seperation.<BR>I'm not driving the system with a gazillion watts but it will be clean and loud enough for me.(50W X 4 for the mains and 200W into an 8" sub)<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||overlord||01-30-2001||03:48 PM||||arg!<BR>thanks man.<BR>I knew it must of been some really easy way...last summer i tried getting measurements for a template...without success.<BR>||||reg||1
